# --- s026 Book I d.3 q.11 = Ord. I d.3 p.3 q.4 (Vat. nn.569-604)
n("n467","s026-01","Vndecima questio tertie distinctionis","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 3 p. 3 q. 4 (Vat. nn. 569–604): *utrum in mente sit distincte imago Trinitatis*. Gorris's first argument (the image is proper to the Word) is not among Scotus's three principal arguments (nn. 569–572). Cf. rather Aug. *De Trin.* VI 2.3 and VII 1.2, and Peter Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 3 c. 2 / d. 27. Gorris's *ad oppositum* (Gen. 1:26) likewise replaces Scotus's (Aug. XIV 8, n. 573), which he uses instead in the reply (¶2).","certain")
n("n468","s026-01","Faciamus hominem ad ymaginem nostram","la","source","Gen. 1:26.","certain")
n("n469","s026-02","Ibi querenda est ymago vbi nihil est melius in natura nostra","la","source","Aug. *De Trin.* XIV 8.11, as quoted at *Ord.* n. 573: *Quaerenda est imago et invenienda ubi nostra natura nihil habet melius*.","certain")
n("n470","s026-02","doctor mouet duo dubia","la","source","*Ord.* nn. 581–582: the doubt about a 'quaternity' in the image, and the doubt about the order of origin. Gorris's references to Henry (*Quodl.* VI qq. 1–2), on the Father's fecundity for spiration remaining (*relicta*) after generation and on the Father begetting *inquantum intelligens*, identify opinions implicit in n. 588 and in Scotus's *Ord.* I d. 2 / d. 7. I have not checked the question numbers.","to-verify")
n("n471","s026-02","relictam ex productione filii","la","textual","A divides the word *de-relictam* across the page break (p. 42/43). The marker is placed inside the word. B has not been checked here.","certain")
n("n472","s026-03","quatuor videbimus","la","commentary","Scotus divides n. 574 into three articles (what an image is; with respect to what in the Trinity; in what it consists in us). Gorris adds a fourth: whether the powers are really distinct from one another and from the essence. This is the issue of Scotus, *Ord.* II d. 16 q. un., which Gorris cites in ¶8.","certain")
n("n473","s026-04","secundum viam Thome prima parte. q. 93. articulo. 6","la","source","Thomas Aquinas, *ST* I q. 93 a. 6: image is found in rational creatures by representation of species, vestige by representation of a trace (*per modum vestigii*). Gorris's formula, image *sub ratione individui* and vestige *sub ratione speciei*, does not reproduce Thomas exactly (Thomas: image *secundum similitudinem speciei*). The passage is absent from Scotus's article (n. 575), which opens directly with 'repraesentativum totius'.","to-verify")
n("n474","s026-04","duo oua similia","la","source","Aug. *De div. quaest. 83*, q. 74, as quoted at *Ord.* n. 575 (*quantumcumque duo ova sint similia, unum non est imago alterius*). The whole paragraph follows n. 575.","certain")
n("n475","s026-05","trinitas constituit conceptum in intellectu nostro","la","source","*Ord.* n. 576, closely paraphrased. Gorris adds the 'numerable whole' with the persons as 'quasi-parts', and the clause *nec respectu illius in quo sunt vnum*.","certain")
n("n476","s026-06","anima habet in se aliquam perfectionem","la","source","*Ord.* n. 580 (*Anima habet in se aliquam perfectionem secundum quam est actus primus respectu notitiae genitae…*). The image consists in first and second acts together.","certain")
n("n477","s026-06","vna substantialitas ratione illarum trium realitatum","la","commentary","*Realitates* is a characteristically Scotist term for the formally distinct perfections of one subject. Cf. *Ord.* II d. 16 (the powers as formally, not really, distinct from the essence, *contentae unitive*).","certain")
n("n478","s026-07","Thome prima parte. q. 77. arti. 8","la","source","The real distinction of the powers from the essence is *ST* I q. 77 a. 1. Their flowing from the essence as proper (inseparable) accidents is q. 77 a. 6. Article 8 concerns the powers remaining in the separated soul, so Gorris's 'a. 8' is inexact (a. 1/6 intended).","certain")
n("n479","s026-07","hec opinio mihi videtur","la","commentary","One of the rare passages in which Gorris argues in the first person, here against Thomas, with Augustine's text in hand.","certain")
n("n480","s026-07","Aug. 10. de tri. c. xi","la","source","Aug. *De Trin.* X 11.18: *Haec igitur tria, memoria, intellegentia, voluntas, quoniam non sunt tres vitae sed una vita, nec tres mentes sed una mens, consequenter utique nec tres substantiae sunt sed una substantia*. The quotation is accurate.","certain")
n("n481","s026-08","doctor in. 2°. dis. 15. in fine","la","source","The question on the distinction of the soul's powers from its essence, and on the image, is Scotus, *Ord.* (and *Rep.*) II d. 16 q. un. (*utrum imago Trinitatis distincte sit in potentiis animae*). 'd. 15' is probably a slip for d. 16, or reflects a different distinction-numbering in Gorris's exemplar.","uncertain")
n("n482","s026-08","proprium verbi quod sit ymago patris","la","source","Cf. Aug. *De Trin.* VI 2.3 and Thomas, *ST* I q. 35 a. 2 (*Imago* as a proper name of the Son). Man is *ad imaginem*, the image of the whole Trinity.","certain")
n("n483","s026-01","in mente sit ymago trinitatis","la","commentary","Later marginalia in brown ink (probably 16th century) at the heads of pp. 42–44 (*Trinitatis ymago*, *filius … deus genuit alium deum* and similar) and beside the articles on p. 43 (*respectu cuius in trinitate*, *in quo in nobis … prima*). They are only partly legible at the resolution of the digitization and are not transcribed.","uncertain")

# --- B collation (full): B39L–B40L
upd("n470", append=" B reads *tria dubia*; A's *duo* agrees with Scotus.")
n("n1107","s026-04","representat quia sub","la","textual","B: *representat sub*, without A's otiose *quia*.","certain")
n("n1108","s026-05","totum numerabile","la","textual","B: *totum materiale*. A's *numerabile* fits the argument (the persons as quasi-parts of a numerable whole) and is kept.","certain")
n("n1109","s026-06","recipit in se noticiam genitam","la","textual","B: *representat in se noticiam genitam*. A's *recipit* matches the Scotist account of intelligence as the power that formally receives the begotten knowledge.","certain")
upd("n477", append=" B: *vna substantialis ratione*.")
n("n1110","s026-06","anime dicitur ymago","la","textual","B: *anime sunt ymago*.","certain")
upd("n480", append=" B reads *c. vij*, which is wrong; A's *xi* is right.")
